> Hi all, small PR for the OTP cleanup job, adds a pause flag so NatCen's job stays paused when Terraform runs. No changes to other environments. Would appreciate a review when you get a chance: https://github.com/ONSdigital/survey-assist-terraform/pull/182


Yes. Run a plan on your ONS machine: first to check the default changes nothing, then with the flag switched on locally to check it would pause the job. Plan only, don't apply.

**1. Get the branch**
```
cd survey-assist-terraform
git fetch
git switch fix/sa-1129-otp-cleanup-pause-flag
```

**2. Check nothing changes by default (sandbox)**
```
cd survey-assist-sandbox
gcloud config set project survey-assist-sandbox
gcloud auth application-default login
terraform init
terraform plan -target=module.firestore-otp
```
You should get "No changes" for the OTP module.

**3. Check the flag works (local only, don't commit)**

Temporarily add this line inside `module "firestore-otp" { ... }` in `survey-assist-sandbox/services.tf`:
```
cloud_run_cli_scheduled_paused = true
```
Then run:
```
terraform plan -target=module.firestore-otp
```
You should see one in-place update, `paused = false -> true`, on `google_cloud_scheduler_job.firestore-otp-cli-scheduled`, with nothing created or destroyed.

**4. Undo the test edit**
```
git checkout services.tf
```

`-target` keeps the plan limited to the OTP module, so it runs quicker. You'll see a warning about `-target`, which is normal. The PR already ran full plans for dev and pre-prod, and they show in the PR checks.
